{"name":"Party Time","hex":"#e3a9c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"party time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A time for entertainment or enjoying oneself.","A season for hosting parties."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/party_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Heptones","blocks":[{"text":"The Heptones are a Jamaican rocksteady and reggae vocal trio most active in the 1960s and early 1970s. They were one of the more significant trios of that era, and played a major role in the gradual transition between ska and rocksteady into reggae with their three-part harmonies. The Heptones were contemporaries of the Wailers and the Maytals, and every bit their equal in the mid-1960s."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Heptones"},{"title":"Party Time (Arnett Cobb album)","blocks":[{"text":"Party Time is an album by saxophonist Arnett Cobb recorded in 1959 for the Prestige label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Party_Time_%28Arnett_Cobb_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party_Time_(Arnett_Cobb_album)"},{"title":"Party Time (ClariS album)","blocks":[{"text":"Party Time is the third studio album by the Japanese pop music duo ClariS, released on June 4, 2014, by SME Records. The album contains 12 music tracks, three of which were previously released on three of ClariS' singles. Three different editions of the album were released: a regular CD version and two limited editions. Party Time was the last time Clara and Alice performed as ClariS, with Alice leaving the duo. Party Time peaked at No. 2 on the Japanese Oricon weekly albums chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Party_Time_%28ClariS%29_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party_Time_(ClariS_album)"},{"title":"Party","blocks":[{"text":"A party is a gathering of people who have been invited by a host for the purposes of socializing, conversation, recreation, or as part of a festival or other commemoration or celebration of a special occasion. A party will often feature food and beverages, and generally conversation, music, dancing, or other forms of entertainment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Hip%2C_Hip%2C_Hurrah%21_Artists%E2%80%99_Party%2C_Skagen_%28Peder_Severin_Kr%C3%B8yer%29_-_Gothenburg_Museum_of_Art_-_F_62.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wi